SUMMARY:"Burning Coal Theatre Presents KidsWrite! Festival 2026"
DESCRIPTION:Every spring Burning Coal Theatre accepts original one-act play submissions for our KidsWrite! series to encourage the young writers of North Carolina! This is a terrific opportunity for budding playwrights to challenge their imagination and bring their stories to life on stage. Finalists have their work professionally produced and performed in front of an audience at Burning Coal Theatre. \nThe 2026 KidsWrite! Festival\, directed by Zoe Matney and Christina Polge\, includes: \nFocus\, by Eliza Basch\nAnd I Feel Fine\, by Jonathan Noah Howard\nToday I Feel Like Death\, by Taite Capes\nHope in Faith\, by Mia Hayes\nA Love Letter\, by Talia Tran\nSplit Screen\, by Simon Payen\nRoulette\, by Neile Joshi\nApollo’s Great Adventure\, by Del Traylor\nKarmic Sickness\, by Samantha Allard
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/burning-coal-theatre-presents-kidswrite-festival-2026/2026-05-29/
LOCATION:Burning Coal Theatre\, 224 Polk St\, Raleigh\, 27604
CATEGORIES:Festival
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://unitedarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/KidsWrite-2026-Social-Media-Comic-Books-Theme.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Burning Coal Theatre":MAILTO:info@burningcoal.org
END:VEVENT
